# libbpf

A BPF Instruction Set Architecture (ISA) interpreter/VM in pedantic C89,
implemented from RFC 9669 (`tmp/rfc9669.txt`).

The deliverable is a strict, portable C89 register-machine interpreter that
decodes, validates, and executes eBPF programs: 11 registers (r0-r10, r10 the
read-only frame pointer), the basic (64-bit) and wide (128-bit) instruction
encodings, ALU/ALU64 arithmetic including signed divide/modulo and byte-swap,
JMP/JMP32 control flow with CALL/EXIT, bounds-checked memory access
(load/store/sign-extension), and 32/64-bit atomic operations.

Conformance groups per RFC 9669 section 7.1: `base32` (mandatory) plus
`base64`, `divmul32`, `divmul64`, `atomic32`, `atomic64` are supported.
The deprecated `packet` group and host-specific 64-bit-immediate subtypes
(`map_fd`/`map_val`/`var_addr`/`code_addr`/`map_idx`/`map_val_idx`) are
rejected as unsupported.

Constraints:
- green profile: strict C89 AND strict C23 under GCC and Clang, green
  semantic checks, canonical Allman format. The gate is currently RED pending
  green compliance work.
- Four-space indentation; Allman braces; 80-column.

Build and test via `just`. The CLI binary is `build/bpf`.

## Recipes

- `just build` — compile the library and `bpf` CLI
- `just test` — run unit + e2e + smoke + C89-probe tests
- `just check` — green gate (currently red)
- `just lint` — shellcheck + clang-format
- `just memcheck` — valgrind memcheck on unit binaries

## Layout

- `src/` — public API (`bpf.h`), decoder, validator, evaluator, CLI
- `test/` — unit + e2e + smoke tests
- `.agent/` — concept, design, stories, scenarios, acceptance
- `tmp/` — reference material (RFC 9669)
